Install docker compose

===========================================================================================================================================================

Oracle/RHEL

1. sudo dnf config-manager --add-repo https://download.docker.com/linux/centos/docker-ce.repo
2. sudo dnf install docker-ce docker-ce-cli containerd.io docker-compose-plugin
3. sudo systemctl enable --now docker
4. newgrp docker
5. sudo usermod -aG docker $USER

===========================================================================================================================================================
Ubuntu/Debian

1. 
DOCKER_CONFIG=${DOCKER_CONFIG:-$HOME/.docker}
mkdir -p $DOCKER_CONFIG/cli-plugins
curl -SL https://github.com/docker/compose/releases/download/v5.2.0/docker-compose-linux-x86_64 -o $DOCKER_CONFIG/cli-plugins/docker-compose
2. chmod +x $DOCKER_CONFIG/cli-plugins/docker-compose
3. docker compose version

Add user to docker group (to code without sudo)

2. newgrp docker

3. sudo usermod -aG docker $USER

4.  Connect SMB using cifs-utils
    sudo apt update
    sudo apt install cifs-utils
    sudo mkdir /mnt/myshare
    sudo mount -t cifs //servername_or_ip/sharename /mnt/myshare -o credentials=/root/.smbcredentials,uid=1000,gid=1000

